  doi = {10.1016/j.neucli.2008.10.001},
  urldate = {2021-05-26},
  abstract = {This paper addresses the question of why voluntary movement, which induces a perturbation to balance, is possible without falling down. It proceeds from a joint biomechanical and physiological approach, and consists of three parts. The first one introduces some basic concepts that constitute a theoretical framework for experimental studies. The second part considers the various categories of ``postural adjustments'' (PAs) and presents major data on ``anticipatory postural adjustments'' (APA). The last part explores the concept of ``posturo-kinetic capacity'' (PKC) and its possible applications. R\'esum\'e Cet article aborde la question de savoir pourquoi le mouvement, qui induit une perturbation de l'\'equilibre corporel, s'av\`ere possible sans entra\^iner de chute. On se situera dans une double perspective associant approche biom\'ecanique et physiologique. La premi\`ere partie introduit quelques concepts de base servant de cadre th\'eorique aux \'etudes exp\'erimentales. La seconde consid\`ere les diverses cat\'egories d'\guillemotleft ~ajustements posturaux~\guillemotright{} et pr\'esente les principales donn\'ees concernant les \guillemotleft ~ajustements posturaux anticipateurs~\guillemotright{} (APA). Enfin, la troisi\`eme partie explore le concept de \guillemotleft ~capacit\'e posturo-cin\'etique~\guillemotright{} (CPC, ou PKC en anglais) et ses possibles applications.},
  langid = {english},
  keywords = {Ajustements posturaux anticipateurs (APAs),Amput\'es de membre inf\'erieur,Anticipatory postural adjustments (APAs),Capacit\'e fococin\'etique (CFC),Capacit\'e posturocin\'etique (CPC),Cha\^ine posturale,Dynamic stability,Foco-kinetic capacity (FKC),Lois de Newton,Lower limb amputees,Mouvement volontaire,Newton's laws,paraplegics,Parapl\'egiques,Postural chain,Postural programming,Postural stabilization,Posturo-kinetic capacity (PKC),Programmation posturale,Stabilisation posturale,Stabilit\'e dynamique,Voluntary movement},
