  abstract = {The acquisition of second language (L2) Spanish suprasegmentals has received very little attention, even less than has the acquisition of Spanish vowels and consonants. This chapter describes the hierarchy of suprasegmental structure in Spanish and introduces areas of empirical research for second language acquisition (SLA). Then, it presents the general principles of first language (L1) and L2 phonology along with an overview of current models of L2 phonological acquisition. Next, the chapter describes the cross-linguistic findings on L2 suprasegmentals. The SLA of Spanish suprasegmentals is addressed, focusing on perception studies, stress, intonation, and rhythm. Finally, the chapter offers direction for future research.},
