  urldate = {2021-02-27},
  abstract = {The computational and robotic synthesis of language evolution is emerging as a new exciting field of research. The objective is to come up with precise operational models of how communities of agents, equipped with a cognitive apparatus, a sensori-motor system, and a body, can arrive at shared grounded communication systems. Such systems may have similar characteristics to animal communication or human language. Apart from its technological interest in building novel applications in the domain of human\textendash robot or robot\textendash robot interaction, this research is of interest to the many disciplines concerned with the origins and evolution of language and communication.},
